<title>CONGO: Zaire foes take talks breather on ship.</title>
<headline>Zaire foes take talks breather on ship.</headline>
<dateline>ON BOARD SAS OUTENIQUA, Congo 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zaire's ailing President Mobutu Sese Seko and rebel leader Laurent Kabila took a break from peace talks on board a South African ship on Sunday, witnesses said.</p>
<p>Reporters on board the SAS Outeniqua said the first session of talks, brokered by South Africa's Nelson Mandela, lasted from 11.55 a.m. (1055 GMT) to 1.17 p.m. (1217 GMT).</p>
</text>
